@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# Fork CI (<sglang-fork>)
+
+This fork runs upstream sglang's GitHub Actions workflows on our own runners,
+on demand only. Everything here is fork-only; upstream never sees it.
+
+## Running a workflow
+
+Upstream's `schedule:` triggers are all stripped. The one schedule left is the
+fork's own: `fork-runner-image.yml` rebuilds the runner image every Monday at
+05:17 UTC (`fork-*.yml` workflows keep their schedules). Start a workflow by hand:
+
+```bash
+gh workflow run <file> -R <sglang-fork> --ref prod [-f key=value]
+# e.g.
+gh workflow run nightly-release-gateway.yml -R <sglang-fork> --ref prod
+gh run list -R <sglang-fork> --workflow nightly-release-gateway.yml
+```
+
+Many upstream jobs keep their `if: github.repository == 'sgl-project/sglang'`
+guard, so they are skipped here even when dispatched.
+
+## Runner labels
+
+`self_hosted_runners.py --apply` rewrites GitHub-hosted labels in every workflow
+that can start in this fork (a `workflow_dispatch`, `workflow_run`,
+`repository_dispatch`, `issues`/`issue_comment` or `push` to `prod` trigger),
+plus the reusable workflows and local actions they call:
+
+| Hosted label                              | Our label            | Where it runs |
+| ----------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ------------- |
+| `ubuntu-latest`, `ubuntu-22.04`, `ubuntu-24.04` | `arc-sglang`   | ARC runner scale set in a self-hosted cluster (installed, listener Running; image: `runner-image/`) |
+| `ubuntu-2x.04-arm`                        | `sglang-linux-arm64` | no runner, by decision (see below) |
+| `macos-latest`, `macos-NN`                | `sglang-macos`       | runner `iris2-sglang` on iris2 (Mac Studio, Apple M4 Max, ARM64; online) |
+| `windows-latest`, `windows-20NN`          | `sglang-windows`     | no runner, by decision (see below) |
+| `${{ matrix.os }}-latest`                 | `fromJSON(...)[matrix.os]` over the three labels above | as above |
+
+`sglang-windows` and `sglang-linux-arm64` have no runner by decision: runners
+for them were declined on 2026-10-27. A dispatched Windows or ARM64 leg queues
+until GitHub expires it, at $0. The labels stay so those legs never fall back
+to GitHub-hosted runners.
+
+The repository also has a $1 Actions budget that stops usage when reached. It
+blocks GitHub-hosted minutes only; jobs on our self-hosted runners are unaffected.
+
+Hardware labels (GPU/AMD/NPU/MLU/MUSA/XPU, e.g. `1-gpu-h100`, `linux-mi300-*`)
+are left as they are: no runner here carries them, so those jobs queue at $0.
+Pull-request-only and push-to-`main` workflows are left untouched.
+
+## Upstream merges
+
+On a conflict in `.github/workflows/**`, take upstream's side, then run
+`python3 .github/fork/self_hosted_runners.py --apply` and commit.
+
+The script only removes schedule triggers and swaps runner labels, so running
+it again is a no-op (`--apply` is idempotent). It removes a `schedule:` key with
+its cron items (indented or at the same column) and the comment block right
+above it, and rewrites `on: schedule`, `on: [..., schedule]` and a `- schedule`
+item of a block-list `on:` (adding `workflow_dispatch` when nothing else is
+left). A form it cannot rewrite (an `on:` flow mapping, a flow list spanning
+lines) makes `--apply` exit 1 with `refused: file:line`; edit that line by hand.
+An unmapped hosted label or an unknown `*-latest` composition is refused the
+same way.
+
+## Guard
+
+`.github/workflows/fork-runner-guard.yml` runs on every push to `prod` that
+touches `.github/**`. It runs `test_self_hosted_runners.py`, then
+`self_hosted_runners.py --check`, which fails listing `file:line` for any
+schedule trigger outside `fork-*.yml`, hosted label or unknown `*-latest`
+composition that came back.
+Locally:
+
+```bash
+python3 .github/fork/test_self_hosted_runners.py && python3 .github/fork/self_hosted_runners.py --check
+```
+
+## Runner image
+
+`runner-image/Dockerfile` is the stock `actions-runner` image plus Python 3,
+build tools and `gh`. Build and push it with the `Fork Runner Image` workflow:
+
+```bash
+gh workflow run fork-runner-image.yml -R <sglang-fork> --ref prod
+```
+
+The run summary prints the pushed digest to pin in the scale set. Each run
+tags its digest `<commit>-<run id>-<run attempt>`, so a digest a pool pins
+never loses its tag, even across re-runs; `<commit>` alone moves to that
+commit's newest build.
diff --git a/.github/fork/runner-image/Dockerfile b/.github/fork/runner-image/Dockerfile
