+    leaves an unset one out of ``model_dump``; xgrammar (0.2.7) maps only
+    ``strict is False`` to unconstrained arguments, so every tool that did not
+    send ``strict`` had its declared schema compiled in, as if strict. That
+    grammar holds an object's declared keys to their declared order: a model
+    writing a declared key out of order can only spell it as an undeclared
+    one, ``"id "`` for ``"id"`` (the padded todo_write keys of #898, from the
+    box-d -> box-e roll). OpenAI reads an omitted ``strict`` as false, and so
+    did this before #46133; an explicit ``strict: true`` keeps its schema."""
+    converted = tool.model_dump()
+    function = converted.get("function")
+    if isinstance(function, dict) and function.get("strict") is None:
