+    """Render ``cut`` into the snapshot's events, one list per frame.
+
+    The first frame opens with ``SnapshotBegin(num_blocks)`` and the last one
+    closes with ``SnapshotEnd(num_blocks)``; in between are the per-page
+    ``BlockStored`` events ``record_store`` would have emitted, coalesced into
+    parent-linked chains exactly as the recorder's queue coalesces them. A
+    frame is closed before the page that would take it past
+    ``max_frame_tokens`` tokens or ``max_frame_pages`` pages (``None``: no
+    bound, so the whole snapshot is one frame -- byte for byte the batch
+    ``record_snapshot`` has always queued). A chain cut by a frame boundary
+    continues in the next frame with its parent link to the last page of the
+    previous one, so the frames concatenated announce the same pages with the
+    same links, and a consumer's window counts the same ``num_blocks``.
+
+    ``pace``, when given, is called every 16 pages: the off-loop renderer uses
+    it to hand the GIL back to the scheduler at a bounded interval.
+
