+    def record_snapshot(self, root: Any, medium=None) -> int:
+        """Re-announce every page of the tree under ``root``, on every tier.
+
+        ``record_store`` and ``record_remove`` are incremental: a consumer that
+        subscribes late sees only what changed afterwards. This walk rebuilds
+        the whole page map in one batch -- ``SnapshotBegin``, the per-page
+        ``BlockStored`` events the store path would have emitted, then
+        ``SnapshotEnd`` -- so a router that just subscribed can index the cache
+        without waiting for another request to touch it.
+
+        The batch is two passes over the tree, so each pass keeps one medium
+        and its parent-linked chains coalesce as they do on the live path:
+
+        * **Device** (``medium``, default ``StorageMedium.GPU``): every page
+          whose KV is on device. A node whose device KV was evicted is not on
+          device, and neither is anything under it, so the pass stops there.
+        * **Host** (``StorageMedium.CPU``, wire ``"CPU_PINNED"``): every page
+          a HiCache host tier holds (``node.backuped``), including the nodes
+          the device evicted -- the host-only pages a resume loads back
+          instead of prefilling. A node whose write-through DMA has not been
+          acknowledged (``write_through_pending_id``) is not announced yet:
+          the live path announces the host copy only at the ack, and the
+          snapshot says no more than the live path would. The pass descends
+          through every node some tier holds, because a write-back host copy
+          may sit under a device-only parent; it stops at a node no tier
+          holds, since nothing under it can be matched.
+
+        A page on both tiers is announced twice, once per medium, exactly as
+        the live path announced it (the device store at insert, the host store
+        at the backup ack); a consumer unions the tiers per page. The count is
+        page *announcements*, which is what a consumer tallies from the
+        ``BlockStored`` events of the window to decide that it is complete.
+        Without a host tier no node is backed up and the batch is the device
+        pass alone, byte for byte.
+
+        ``root`` itself is not announced: its key is empty and it holds no
+        pages.
