+"""Chat preprocessing lanes: a cheap request never waits behind a giant conversion.
+
+Part 0021 converted every ``/v1/chat/completions`` and ``/v1/messages`` request
+on ONE worker thread. On box-c (#6667, 2026-09-28 22:44-23:13Z) requests with a
+cheap prefill timed out behind 480k-930k-token prompts: each giant held the one
+worker for seconds, and everything queued behind it reached the scheduler late.
+
+``preprocess_lanes`` gives the conversion two lanes: a small lane of
+``SGLANG_CHAT_PREPROCESS_WORKERS`` threads and a giant lane for conversions of
+``SGLANG_CHAT_PREPROCESS_GIANT_CHARS`` characters or more. With more than one
+thread, every conversion uses a private tokenizer copy. Every conversion's
+lane, queue, wait and run time are logged and exported, and the event loop's
+lag and Python's GC pauses are measured.
+
+What these tests pin (each with its negative control):
+
+* a small conversion completes while a giant one is held on the giant lane;
+  with one lane and one worker (0021) it waits for the giant;
+* the small lane runs its workers in parallel, each with its own tokenizer
+  copy, never the manager's own and never two threads on one copy; one
+  worker (0021) converts on the manager's own tokenizer, one at a time;
+* a copy isolates tokenizer state: a truncation change on one worker does
+  not wait for (or raise against) another worker's encode, where on one
+  shared real fast tokenizer it does;
+* the request reaching the scheduler is identical to the inline conversion's,
+  from both lanes and both facades, with a real fast tokenizer;
+* a tokenizer that cannot be copied is shared, one conversion at a time;
+* each conversion's queue, wait and run are logged and exported per lane;
+  a queued conversion whose caller is cancelled never runs;
+* the event-loop lag monitor reports a blocked loop, and GC pauses are timed.
+
+No server, no GPU: the real ``OpenAIServingChat`` (dsv41, box-c's path) and
+``AnthropicServing`` over a stub tokenizer manager.
+"""
+
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import asyncio
+import gc
+import logging
+import threading
+import time
+from typing import Dict, List, Optional
+from unittest import mock
